{
  "schema": "iralens-benchmark-urls/1",
  "frozen": "2026-10-11",
  "notes": [
    "100 public URLs across news, docs, wikis, blogs, JS-heavy apps, PDFs and",
    "walled pages. A read passes when the extracted main text contains",
    "required_phrase (whitespace/case-insensitive).",
    "expect=phrase_or_walled marks pages that may legitimately refuse (paywall,",
    "login wall): those pass with the phrase OR with a typed error \u2014 never with",
    "silently empty content. See run_benchmark.py for the exact scoring.",
    "requires_js=True marks pages whose useful text is rendered client-side; if",
    "the static fetch does not contain the phrase, the read must fall back to the",
    "browser engine automatically."
